From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Serge A. Salamanka" <ssalamanka@scnsoft.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:07:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] data-import: offer to copy stock Kiro Crew's home on first
 run

A distribution whose data home is not upstream's is usually installed
next to stock Kiro Crew. On its first run (its own home absent, the
stock home's config.json present) the CLI, in an interactive terminal,
and the desktop shell, before the gateway starts, ask once whether to
copy that home. Import skips the other install's pid, lock and socket
files and kirocrew-bin/, points dashboard.url at this product's own
default port, and is refused while the stock gateway answers. Start
fresh creates the empty home so the question never comes back.
Upstream never asks.

